    "Church fair (Kerwe) as the crown of rural festivals (Platzburschen, dancing, food), discontinued village festivals; start of the folk calendar: January (New Year, Epiphany, Fabian and Sebastian, Conversion of Paul) and February (Candlemas, change of servants, Shrovetide).",
